they are not necessarily equivalent. One method would be to use a two-dimensional array of type CV32FC1 with n rows and three columns (n-by-3). Similarly, you could use a
two-dimensional array with three rows and n columns (3-by-n). You could also use an
array with n rows and one column (n-by-1) of type CV32FC3 or an array with one row and
n columns (3-by-1). Some of these cases can be freely converted from one to the other
(meaning you can just pass one where the other is expected) but others cannot. To understand why, consider the memory layout shown in Figure 3-2.
